course: dictionary
lesson: 15526
title: Words that go underground
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words can look scary, but you can break them into parts. «Sub-» means under, and «terra» means earth, as in «terrain» and «territory». Put them together and «subterranean» means under the earth.
explain: Read this sentence: «Scientists found a subterranean river deep inside the cave.» The clue is deep inside the cave. A river that is deep inside a cave must be under the ground, so subterranean means underground.
explain: Sometimes the word is used in a more formal way to mean hidden or secret. «The spy escaped through a subterranean passage that nobody else knew about.» The passage is hidden, not just underground. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «underground» or «secret» still make sense? Then you know.
fact: «Subterranean» means underground, below the surface of the earth.
fact: «Subterranean» can also mean hidden or secret, in a formal style.
fact: «Sub-» means under, and «terra» means earth, as in «terrain» and «territory».
fact: Subterranean rivers, caves and tunnels are studied in science and geography, and some animals, such as moles and blind cave fish, live underground.
exercise: «The moles dig long subterranean tunnels under the garden.» What does subterranean mean here? | Very tall | Covered in snow | Made of glass | *Underground
exercise: In the word subterranean, which part means under? | nean | *sub | terra | rain
exercise: «The hidden door led to a subterranean passage, and nobody knew where it went.» Which meaning fits best here? | Full of music | *Hidden or secret, and underground | Bright and sunny | Very wet and cold
test: «Scientists found blind fish living in a subterranean river.» Where do the fish live? | On a sunny beach | *Underground, in a river | Up in the trees | In a busy shop
test: Which word from the same family as subterranean means the ground you walk over? | sunshine | tunnel | *terrain | river
exam: Tom says subterranean means very loud. Is he right? | Yes, it means loud and noisy | No, it means very wet | Yes, it means bright and shiny | *No, it means underground, below the surface of the earth
